The importance of mobile safety inspections in mining
Mining workplaces are geographically dispersed and operationally dynamic.

Inspection teams may need to examine haul roads, workshops, processing plants, conveyor systems, underground workings and contractor work areas.

Paper-based inspections can delay the visibility of critical findings, particularly when information must be transferred manually into a separate action register.

Mobile inspection workflows can help capture findings, photographs, location information and assigned actions closer to the point of observation.

