Contractor safety: Managing risk across multiple employers
Mining operations frequently depend on contractors for drilling, blasting, equipment maintenance, construction, transport and specialist services.

Contractor safety should not operate as a separate administrative process.

Contractors need appropriate induction, competency verification, risk communication, work authorization and supervision.

Incident and near-miss information should be available to authorized teams responsible for identifying common risks across employers and work areas.

For example, if several contractors experience similar isolation failures, the mine should examine whether a site-wide control weakness exists rather than treating each event independently.

